   "evidence": "Line 44: `/-- The integral Cartan matrix, specialized to the coefficient ring. -/ abbrev matrix ... := !![0, -1; 1, -1]`. The module docstring itself describes this matrix as an action on the Cartan part of a root-free reductive datum, not as a Cartan matrix.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/FixedSubmodule/OrderThree.lean",
   "fix": "Reword it, e.g. \"The matrix `[[0,-1],[1,-1]]` of the order-three automorphism of the rank-two cocharacter lattice, with entries in `R`.\"",
   "issue": "The docstring calls `!![0, -1; 1, -1]` \"The integral Cartan matrix\". \"Cartan matrix\" is a standard Lie-theory term for the matrix of pairings between roots and coroots; for type A\u2082 that is `[[2,-1],[-1,2]]`. This matrix is instead an order-three automorphism of the rank-two cocharacter lattice. The docstring also says \"integral\" for a matrix whose entries are taken in an arbitrary ring `R`.",
   "line": 44
  }
